# PACT — environment
#
# Every value here is OPTIONAL. `npm run dev` with no .env at all gives you a fully
# working app: the in-process store is seeded with the demo scenarios, and the Pact
# Builder falls back to a deterministic reader when no model is configured.
#
# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in only what you need.

# --- Sessions ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# HMAC key for the signed session cookie. Optional in development (one is generated per
# server start, so sessions reset on restart). REQUIRED in production, minimum 32 chars —
# the app refuses to start without it rather than silently minting cookies with a random
# per-instance secret that every other instance would reject.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- AI ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Powers the Pact Builder, Smart Review and Explain This Pact.
# Set EITHER a Gemini key OR an Anthropic key — Gemini is preferred when both are present
# because it has a free tier. With neither, those features still work using
# lib/ai/fallback.ts, and the UI says so rather than implying a model wrote the output.
#
# Server-side only. Neither key is ever sent to the browser.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set both to use Postgres; leave blank to use the in-process store.
#
# The schema lives in a dedicated `pact` schema (see supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql),
# so it can share a Supabase project with another app without colliding with anything.
#
# The service role key bypasses row level security by design — PACT's own server routes
# do the authorisation. Never expose it to the browser and never commit it.
# Find it in: Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API → service_role
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
